.TH HMAP_GET 3 "15 Mar 2023" "CB" "Library Functions"

.SH NAME
hmap_get \- Retrieve data associated with a key from a hash map

.SH SYNOPSIS
.IB #include <lib/hmap.h>

.IB void*
.IB hmap_get(HMAP_DB* db, const char* key, size_t keylen);

.SH DESCRIPTION
The \fBhmap_get\fR function retrieves the data associated with a key from a hash map. It takes a pointer to the hash map database, a key, and the length of the key as arguments.

The function takes the following parameters:
.IB HMAP_DB*
A pointer to the hash map database.
.IB const char*
The key whose data needs to be retrieved.
.IB size_t
The length of the key.

The function returns a pointer to the data associated with the key. If the key is not found, it returns \fBNULL\fB.

The \fBhmap_get\fR function is intended to be used to retrieve data from a hash map based on a key.

.SH EXAMPLES
The following example demonstrates how to use the \fBhmap_get\fR function to retrieve data from a hash map:

.nf
#include <stdio.h>
#include <lib/hmap.h>

int main() {
    HMAP_DB* hmap_db;
    // Initialize the hash map database
    hmap_init(&hmap_db);

    // Add a tuple with a string data type
    hmap_add_tuple_with_data(&hmap_db, "example1", 8, "data1");

    // Retrieve the data associated with the key "example1"
    const char* data = hmap_get(hmap_db, "example1", 8);

    if(data != NULL) {
        printf("Retrieved data: %s\n", data);
    } else {
        printf("Key not found\n");
    }

    // Free the hash map database
    hmap_destroy(&hmap_db);

    return 0;
}
.nef